<ReportItem port="6667" svc_name="irc" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="46882" pluginName="UnrealIRCd Backdoor Detection" pluginFamily="Backdoors">
<description>The remote IRC server is a version of UnrealIRCd with a backdoor that allows an attacker to execute arbitrary commands on the affected host. The service runs as root, so the backdoor grants root-level command execution.</description>
<synopsis>The remote IRC server contains a backdoor allowing arbitrary code execution.</synopsis>
<solution>Re-download the software, verify it using the published MD5/SHA1 checksums, and re-install it. Run the service under a non-privileged account.</solution>
<cvss_base_score>10.0</cvss_base_score>
<cve>CVE-2010-2075</cve>
</ReportItem>

<ReportItem port="5900" svc_name="vnc" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="61708" pluginName="VNC Server 'password' Password" pluginFamily="Gain a shell remotely">
<description>The VNC server running on the remote host is secured with a weak password. Nessus was able to login using VNC authentication and a password of 'password'. A remote, unauthenticated attacker could exploit this to take control of the system.</description>
<synopsis>The remote VNC server is protected with a weak password.</synopsis>
<solution>Secure the VNC service with a strong password.</solution>
<cvss_base_score>10.0</cvss_base_score>
</ReportItem>

<ReportItem port="22" svc_name="ssh" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="32321" pluginName="Debian OpenSSH/OpenSSL Package Random Number Generator Weakness" pluginFamily="Gain a shell remotely">
<description>The remote host is affected by a flaw in the Debian OpenSSL package: a weak random number generator makes SSH/SSL keys predictable. An attacker can brute-force the private key and gain access.</description>
<synopsis>The remote SSH host keys are predictable.</synopsis>
<solution>Regenerate any weak keys using a fixed version of the OpenSSL library.</solution>
<cvss_base_score>10.0</cvss_base_score>
<cve>CVE-2008-0166</cve>
</ReportItem>

